WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.040
This update describes release four three
one zero one six c.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.671
Watch it before the November seventh
update and the dated November fifth

00:00:07.671 --> 00:00:08.978
course.

00:00:08.978 --> 00:00:13.978
It covers hospital consent purposes,
integrations with health record systems,

00:00:13.978 --> 00:00:19.490
additional languages, and security changes
that operators should understand.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:24.430
These cards explain the workflow; they are
not recordings of clicks.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.478
Practise only with invented records.

00:00:27.478 --> 00:00:32.038
A hospital deployment still requires
commissioning, approved notices and live

00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:33.649
providers.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:39.028
A privacy officer can now draft a hospital
purpose under one of the five base

00:00:39.028 --> 00:00:43.216
purposes, with its own notice wording in
each language.

00:00:43.216 --> 00:00:48.050
A different privacy officer must confirm
the translations were reviewed and approve

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.180
it.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:54.240
A scoped purpose can only narrow its base
purpose, never widen it.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.978
Reception records each purpose as a
separate choice, and patients can withdraw

00:00:58.978 --> 00:01:02.109
one purpose without touching the others.

00:01:02.109 --> 00:01:07.587
Retiring a purpose stops new choices;
earlier records stay in history.

00:01:08.308 --> 00:01:12.903
The hospital record system can now ask
CareConsent for the current allow or deny

00:01:12.903 --> 00:01:17.436
decision through a signed request, and
receives a signed answer.

00:01:17.436 --> 00:01:22.900
Requests outside the time window or
repeating a used value are refused.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:27.377
Connected systems can authenticate with
SMART backend services using a signed

00:01:27.377 --> 00:01:28.972
client key.

00:01:28.972 --> 00:01:35.031
The ABDM bridge supports mock and sandbox
modes and verifies gateway signatures.

00:01:35.031 --> 00:01:39.972
Your vendor's adapter must still enforce
the decision where records are opened, and

00:01:39.972 --> 00:01:44.040
ABDM use needs National Health Authority
onboarding.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:47.788
The pilot languages remain reviewed.

00:01:47.788 --> 00:01:52.931
Fifteen further Indian languages now have
draft messages and patient PDFs using

00:01:52.931 --> 00:01:55.490
bundled fonts for each script.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:59.931
A draft language is not sent to patients
until a named reviewer records an

00:01:59.931 --> 00:02:02.728
attestation that the wording was checked.

00:02:02.728 --> 00:02:06.990
Until then, those patients receive English
messages.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:11.693
Ask your hospital's approved translator to
review the wording, and report any

00:02:11.693 --> 00:02:16.396
confusing phrase rather than editing it
during a patient conversation.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.490
Sign-in and session records are now
isolated per hospital.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:26.942
Configured keys must be full random keys;
passphrases are rejected, and webhooks use

00:02:26.942 --> 00:02:30.907
their own key instead of reusing the
multi-factor key.

00:02:30.907 --> 00:02:35.585
Each audit entry's hash now covers the
branch, the person acting and the affected

00:02:35.585 --> 00:02:36.930
record.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:42.442
Recorded security events cannot be edited
or deleted by the application.

00:02:42.442 --> 00:02:47.240
Webhooks to private network addresses are
blocked, including names that resolve to

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.442
them.

00:02:48.442 --> 00:02:53.026
If a configuration is refused at startup,
correct it rather than weakening the

00:02:53.026 --> 00:02:54.392
setting.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:03:00.100
A deployment can now require its symmetric
keys to be sealed by a hardware security

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:04.942
module, so plain key material is not
stored in configuration.

00:03:04.942 --> 00:03:09.359
Signed audit log heads can be published
automatically to separately owned

00:03:09.359 --> 00:03:14.204
immutable storage and re-verified later,
which helps show that history was not

00:03:14.204 --> 00:03:15.550
rewritten.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:20.454
The security monitor refuses the hospital
or migration database connection and

00:03:20.454 --> 00:03:24.050
checks it is running under its own
database role.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:28.985
Your team must provision the real key
vault, storage and monitor role.

00:03:29.725 --> 00:03:34.225
Everyday reception, patient withdrawal,
breach handling and offline branch

00:03:34.225 --> 00:03:38.651
workflows continue as taught in the
earlier update and course.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:43.734
Board filings now need the actual filing
time and a staff attestation, and guardian

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:48.436
records need explicit verification before
they can support consent.

00:03:48.436 --> 00:03:52.984
This release was tested locally with
synthetic data; it is not a hospital

00:03:52.984 --> 00:03:56.615
production approval or a compliance
certificate.

00:03:56.615 --> 00:04:01.782
Before real use, your team must commission
providers, hosting, translations,

00:04:01.782 --> 00:04:05.194
integrations and an independent
assessment.
